        "label": "Treated, alcohol index by Region, Segment, Gender, Age and Year",
        "source": "The National Board of Health and Welfare",
        "updated": "2025-07-10T07:10:00Z",
        "note": [
          "Indicator definition: Number of treated patients in accordance with the patient register (inpatient care or inpatient and/or specialised outpatient care) with explicit alcohol diagnosis (ICD-10: E24.4, F10, G31.2, G62.1, G72.1, I42.6, K29.2, K70, K85.2, K86.0, O35.4, P04.3, Q86.0, T51, Y90.1–Y90.9, Y91.1–Y91.9, Z50.2, Z71.4 and Z72.1) as main or secondary diagnosis per 100,000 inhabitants aged 15 or older. The data are age-standardised with the national average population during 2021 as the standard population. The indicator is reported annually (inpatient care from year 2000, inpatient and/or specialised outpatient care from year 2006) at country and county level (the county in which the patient was registered during the first hospital admission for the relevant diagnoses) and can be disaggregated by gender and age group."
